-- V8: the owner's four abroad-source workbooks, reduced to what actually collects.
--
-- APPLIED LIVE on 2026-09-05 in six parts (seed_foreign_event_sources_v8_part1_at,
-- _part2_cz, _part3_cz_de, _part4_de_pl, _part5_pl_si, _part6_si_sk, plus _part10 for the
-- two Slovak rows that went first). This file is the consolidated record of those rows.
-- A few notes were tightened while applying, so the live table is authoritative for prose;
-- re-running this file is a no-op, thanks to the host guard and ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING.
--
-- Input was 907 rows across four files. 'abroad sources.xlsx' proved to be a genuine
-- superset of the three per-country files (verified: zero endpoints in them that it does
-- not contain), so everything below comes from it.
--
-- The funnel, every step measured rather than assumed:
--   907  rows in the workbooks
--   533  unique endpoints -- the German sheet alone repeats germany.travel 195 times and
--        eventfinder.de 117 times, so its 500 rows are really 184 endpoints
--   515  not already in the registry, deduped on HOST per the V5 lesson
--   154  survived a mechanical live probe with our own honest fetcher
--    85  accepted by the first judging pass
--    74  still accepted after an adversarial second pass  <- all registered below
--    41  collect events when the REAL worker extractor is pointed at them  <- scrape_enabled
--
-- Why that last line is the one that matters: all 14 V6 sources passed two judging passes
-- and twelve then collected nothing. A source is proven by a run, never by a source row.
-- Every row below was run through the worker's own extractor and carries the count it
-- produced on 2026-09-05, with real event titles, in parser_strategy.
--
-- The 33 rows with scrape_enabled=false are NOT failures of vetting -- two independent
-- passes read each listing and named real future events on it. They are failures of our
-- GENERIC extractor, and each row says what it needs. Registering them keeps the endpoint
-- and its robots clearance; visitberlin.de, visitczechia.com, deutscheoperberlin.de and
-- eventfrog.at are the highest-value recipes waiting to be written. This follows the
-- wien.info precedent set in V7.
--
-- WHAT THE WORKBOOKS GOT WRONG, worth knowing for the next batch:
--   151 of the 515 candidate URLs were plain HTTP 404.
--    46 more had no working host at all (NXDOMAIN, expired or self-signed certificates,
--       connect timeouts) and did not recover on a retry with a longer timeout.
--    33 of the 72 rows the judges rejected were A SINGLE EVENT rather than an event
--       listing -- one festival, one marathon, one trade fair. Germany was worst hit
--       (14 of its 29 rejects).
--    10 more listed only past events.
--
-- The second pass earned its place again, killing 8 of 85 first-pass accepts: empty JS
-- shells whose calendars never render, a soft-404, a single festival's editorial date
-- article, and a commercial trade-fair feed dressed as heritage culture. 60 of the 74
-- accepted rows also had their endpoint CORRECTED by one of the passes -- the workbook URL
-- was usually not the listing URL.
--
-- TWO OF OUR OWN MISTAKES, both caught by measurement rather than by review:
--   * The first probe ran against a half-built DE locale (EVENT_PATH_WORDS had DE,
--     MONTH_WORDS did not), so localeFor('DE') returned a locale whose months were
--     undefined and threw. That wrongly rejected 64 German candidates; re-probing
--     recovered 25 of them.
--   * shmf.de was first measured with the RENDER strategy against a text/calendar
--     endpoint and 'failed'. Re-measured through the ics strategy it actually declares,
--     it returns three real concerts, so it is enabled. Test a source with the strategy
--     it claims, not with the default.
--
-- robots.txt was fetched for all 74 accepted hosts on 2026-09-05: every path is allowed.
-- Four declare a Crawl-delay (stantonamarlberg.com 10s, visitkoper.si 5s,
-- kultura.poznan.pl 2s, schwerin.de 1s); the worker honours it, and above 5s it drops to
-- listing-only. NOTE: several files carry an EMPTY 'Disallow:' line, which PERMITS
-- everything -- it was parsed, not eyeballed, precisely because it reads like the opposite.
--
-- review_state and legal_review_status are 'approved' because two independent live passes
-- read the page and its robots.txt. `enabled` stays false -- that column drives the legacy
-- no-JS feed pipeline; the Playwright worker reads scrape_enabled.
--
-- Registered per country (enabled / total), with events produced in the proving run:
--   AT:  6 enabled of  8 registered,  168 future-dated events
--   CZ:  8 enabled of 15 registered,  210 future-dated events
--   DE:  9 enabled of 16 registered,  223 future-dated events
--   PL:  5 enabled of  8 registered,  140 future-dated events
--   SI: 13 enabled of 22 registered,  400 future-dated events
--   SK:  0 enabled of  5 registered,    0 future-dated events
--
-- Slovakia lands five rows and zero enabled: every Slovak listing that survived vetting
-- needs a recipe. That is an honest zero, not an omission.

INSERT INTO public.external_event_feed_sources (
  source_id, publisher_name, publisher_type, city, country_code, endpoint_url,
  original_endpoint_url, format, categories, legal_basis, audit_status,
  dedupe_priority, parser_strategy, notes, fetch_hosts,
  review_state, legal_review_status, robots_allowed, enabled, scrape_enabled, scrape_strategy
)
SELECT
  v.source_id, v.publisher_name, NULL, v.city, v.country_code, v.endpoint_url,
  v.endpoint_url, v.format, v.categories, v.legal_basis, NULL,
  v.dedupe_priority, v.parser_strategy,
  'From the owner-supplied 2026-09-05 abroad-sources workbooks; probed with our own honest fetcher, judged and adversarially re-judged live, then proven (or not) by running the real worker extractor.',
  ARRAY[v.host],
  'approved', 'approved', true, false, v.scrape_enabled, v.scrape_strategy
FROM (VALUES

  -- ---------- AT: 6 enabled of 8 ----------
  ('Brucknerhaus Linz (LIVA – Linzer Veranstaltungsgesellschaft, the city''s concert hall)','Linz','AT','https://www.brucknerhaus.at/programm/veranstaltungen','A paginated, filterable programme listing of the concert hall''s own events, each card showing weekday, date, time, hall and title in the raw HTML.',ARRAY['orchestermusik','kammermusik','klaviermusik','orgelmusik','vokalmusik','jazz','kabarett','tanz'],'robots.txt fetched from https://www.brucknerhaus.at/robots.txt on 2026-09-05 (HTTP 200). Rules read: User-agent: * / Disallow: /backend / Disallow: /backend_admin / Sitemap: https://www.brucknerhaus.at/sitemap.xml. The endpoint path is permitted, and no Crawl-delay is declared. https://www.brucknerhaus.at/robots.txt: ''User-agent: *'' / ''Disallow: /backend'' / ''Disallow: /backend_admin'' / ''Sitemap: https://www.brucknerhaus.at/sitemap.xml''. The programme paths are not disallowed. Two independent live passes read this listing and its robots.txt. Collect factual fields only (title, date, time, venue, city, detail URL) and deep-link back; editorial descriptions and photographs stay the publisher''s copyright.',1,'Measured locally on 2026-09-05 with the real worker extractor: 46 future-dated events, 44 distinct titles. Examples it actually returned: "KLANGWOLKEN 26 Kin­der Klang­wol­ke 26 präsentiert von SPARKASSE OÖ & LINZ AG" "KLANGWOLKEN 26 Klang­wol­ken­wo­che" "KLANGWOLKENWOCHE Adal­bert Stif­ter und die End­lich­keit Lesung". Read https://www.brucknerhaus.at/programm/veranstaltungen (HTTP 200, 325,868 bytes) and the given URL''s redirect target https://www.brucknerhaus.at/en/programme/events (HTTP 200, 316,947 bytes). Titles with dates seen in the raw HTML: ''Kinder Klangwolke 26 präsentiert von SPARKASSE OÖ & LINZ AG'' — So, 6. Sep 26, 16:00, Donaupark Linz; ''Linzer Klangwolke 26'' — Sa 12. Sep 26, 20:30, Donaupark Linz; ''Brad Mehldau & Kirill Gerstein – Musical Dialogues in Concert'' — Mo 14. Sep 26, 19:30, Großer Saal. Also ''Festakt 2026'' Su 13. Sep 26 10:30 and ''Poschner, Rondeau & Bruckner Orchester Linz'' Su 13. Sep 26 18:00. SECOND PASS CONFIRMED: Fetched https://www.brucknerhaus.at/programm/veranstaltungen (HTTP 200, 325,868 bytes) myself. Titles and dates I saw, in page order:…','www.brucknerhaus.at','src_8c477a42',true,'render'),
  ('Eventfrog','Österreich','AT','https://eventfrog.at/de/events.html','A nationwide, filterable event-search results page listing individual dated events (plus multi-date ''Event group'' rows) as server-rendered cards.',ARRAY['konzerte','partys','theater & bühne','kunst & ausstellungen','festivals','kinderveranstaltungen','sport & fitness','kurse & seminare'],'robots.txt fetched from https://eventfrog.at/robots.txt on 2026-09-05 (HTTP 200). Rules read: User-agent:* / Disallow: /admin/ / Disallow: /*cockpitv3/ / Disallow: /*account/ / Disallow: /*preview/ / Disallow: /*shop/ / Disallow: /*.pdf$ / Disallow: /*country-redirect/ / Allow: /help/* / Allow: /fr/ / Allow: /en/ / Disallow: /it/ / User-agent: BLEXBot / Disallow: /. The endpoint path is permitted, and no Crawl-delay is declared. https://eventfrog.at/robots.txt: ''User-agent:*'' / ''Disallow: /admin/'' / ''Disallow: /*cockpitv3/'' / ''Disallow: /*account/'' / ''Disallow: /*preview/'' / ''Disallow: /*shop/'' / ''Disallow: /*.pdf$'' / ''Disallow: /*country-redirect/''; then ''Allow: /fr/'' / ''Allow: /en/'' / ''Disallow: /it/''. Neither /de/events.html nor /en/events.html is disallowed. Two independent live passes read this listing and its robots.txt. Collect factual fields only (title, date, time, venue,…',1,'NOT ENABLED: both judging passes accepted this listing, but our extractor collected ZERO future-dated events from it on 2026-09-05. Registered so the endpoint and its robots clearance are not lost; it needs a selector recipe before it can be switched on. Read https://eventfrog.at/de/events.html (HTTP 200, 520,590 bytes) and https://eventfrog.at/en/events.html (HTTP 200, 493,754 bytes). Real titles with dates in the raw HTML: ''ÖSlam 2026 – Österr. Poetry-Slam-Meisterschaften'' — 05 September 2026, Saturday, 19:30, Stadttheater Klagenfurt; ''Maturaball HIB Saalfelden'' — Fri 18. September 2026, 19:00, Saalfelden am Steinernen Meer; ''Padel & Pilates - So Social'' — Sat 10. October 2026, 10:00, Padelzone CampusVäre Dornbirn. Also ''Antonio Vivaldi: Four Seasons by Mystery Ensemble'' 05.09.2026 20:00, Congress Graz. SECOND PASS CONFIRMED: From my own fetch of https://eventfrog.at/de/events.html: ''Antonio Vivaldi: Four Seasons by Mystery Ensemble'' — Samstag, 05. September, 20:00, Congress Graz, Graz (I pulled the exact markup: infos__title ''Antonio Vivaldi: Four Seasons by Mystery Ensemble'',…','eventfrog.at','src_534df272',false,'render'),
  ('Ferienregion Dachstein Salzkammergut – ''Im Salzkammergut'' (UNESCO World Heritage region tourist board: Hallstatt, Bad Goisern, Gosau, Obertraun)','Salzkammergut','AT','https://www.im-salzkammergut.at/veranstaltungen/','A day-by-day regional event calendar listing guided tours, exhibitions, markets, festivals and sport events as server-rendered cards.',ARRAY['führungen','ausstellungen','wanderungen','konzerte','brauchtum','märkte','familie','sport'],'robots.txt fetched from https://www.im-salzkammergut.at/robots.txt on 2026-09-05 (HTTP 200). Rules read: User-agent: * / Disallow: /jsparty/ / Disallow: /sapphire/ / Disallow: /cms/. The endpoint path is permitted, and no Crawl-delay is declared. https://www.im-salzkammergut.at/robots.txt: ''User-agent: *'' / ''Disallow: /jsparty/'' / ''Disallow: /sapphire/'' / ''Disallow: /cms/''. /veranstaltungen/ and /events/ are not disallowed. Two independent live passes read this listing and its robots.txt. Collect factual fields only (title, date, time, venue, city, detail URL) and deep-link back; editorial descriptions and photographs stay the publisher''s copyright.',1,'Measured locally on 2026-09-05 with the real worker extractor: 27 future-dated events, 22 distinct titles. Examples it actually returned: "Einzigartiges Höhlenerlebnis: Führung durch die Koppenbrüllerhöhle in Obertraun" "Krasse Strecken, coole Guides: Täglich "Geführte Mountainbike-Touren" im Salzkammergut" "Führungen durch die “Mammuthöhle“ in Obertraun". Read https://www.im-salzkammergut.at/veranstaltungen/ (HTTP 200, 220,835 bytes). Titles with dates in the raw HTML: ''Führung durch die Dachstein Eishöhle'' — Sa, 5. Sep. 2026, Dachstein-Rieseneishöhle, Obertraun; ''Zeitgeschichte mit spitzer Feder: Cartoon-Ausstellung "Graphic Novel" in Altaussee'' — Sa, 5. Sep. 2026, 09:00–16:00, Salzwelten Altaussee; ''"Obertrauner Bergerlebnis 2026" Sonnenaufgang am Krippenstein mit Bergfrühstück'' — Sa, 5. Sep. 2026, 05:30–09:30, Dachstein-Krippenstein-Seilbahn. The homepage itself also links dated items such as ''Internationaler Wolfgangsee-Lauf / Salzkammergut Marathon''. SECOND PASS CONFIRMED: From my own fetch of https://www.im-salzkammergut.at/veranstaltungen/: ''Führung durch die Dachstein…','www.im-salzkammergut.at','src_548f6cd6',true,'render'),
  ('Kitzbühel Tourismus (Tourismusverband Kitzbühel)','Kitzbühel','AT','https://www.kitzbuehel.com/events/eventkalender/','A filterable town/region event calendar whose cards carry day-badge, full date range, start time and venue in the raw HTML, with a ''load more'' pager.',ARRAY['ausstellungen','konzerte','sport','kulinarik','führungen','brauchtum','familie'],'robots.txt fetched from https://www.kitzbuehel.com/robots.txt on 2026-09-05 (HTTP 200). Rules read: User-Agent: * / Disallow: / Disallow: /wx-tools/ / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbuehel.com/sitemap.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbuehel.com/en/sitemap.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbuehel.com/imagesitemap.xml. The endpoint path is permitted, and no Crawl-delay is declared. https://www.kitzbuehel.com/robots.txt: ''User-Agent: *'' / ''Disallow:'' / ''Disallow: /wx-tools/'' plus three Sitemap lines. Only /wx-tools/ is blocked; the event calendar is allowed. Two independent live passes read this listing and its robots.txt. Collect factual fields only (title, date, time, venue, city, detail URL) and deep-link back; editorial descriptions and photographs stay the publisher''s copyright.',1,'Measured locally on 2026-09-05 with the real worker extractor: 25 future-dated events, 25 distinct titles. Examples it actually returned: "Kunstkino - SO KLINGT DAS LEBEN" "05 SEPT. Ausstellung "summer is calling" Donnerstag 04. Juni bis 30. September 2026 ab 09:" "05 SEPT. Kitz Mountain Guiding Montag 15. Juni bis 04. Oktober 2026 ab 09:30 Kitzbüheler B". Read https://www.kitzbuehel.com/events/eventkalender/ (HTTP 200, 624,859 bytes) and https://www.kitzbuehel.com/en/events/event-calendar/ (HTTP 200, 614,730 bytes). Real titles with dates: ''41. Rotary Rad WM 2026'' — Mittwoch 02. bis 06. September 2026, ab 08:00, Kitzbühel und Umgebung; ''Horngipfelfrühstück mit Sonnenaufgang'' — Sonntag 06. September 2026, ab 05:45, Kitzbüheler Horn; ''Austrian Beach Volleyball Championships'' — Thursday 10. to 13. September 2026, from 09:00, Tennisstadion Kitzbühel. Also ''Kitzbüheler Genussmarkt'' Samstag 08. August bis 31. Oktober 2026. SECOND PASS CONFIRMED: From my own fetch of https://www.kitzbuehel.com/events/eventkalender/, all three of the reviewer''s examples verified in the raw HTML by grep:…','www.kitzbuehel.com','src_1154ecb7',true,'render'),
  ('Kitzbüheler Alpen (regional tourism marketing for Brixental, Hohe Salve, St. Johann in Tirol and Pillerseetal)','Kitzbüheler Alpen','AT','https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/de/kam/events.html','A regional event calendar page whose cards are each backed by a schema.org Event/SportsEvent ld+json block in the raw HTML.',ARRAY['musik','sport','feste / feiern','familie','volkskultur / brauchtum / märkte','theater / show / tanz / film / kleinkunst','wochenprogramm'],'robots.txt fetched from https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/robots.txt on 2026-09-05 (HTTP 200). Rules read: User-Agent: * / Allow: / / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/sitemap.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/de/accommodations.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/de/events.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/de/infrastructure.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/de/v2/tours.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/en/accommodations.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/en/events.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/en/infrastructure.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/en/v2/tours.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/nl/accommodations.xml / Sitemap: https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/nl/events.xml / Sitemap:…',1,'Measured locally on 2026-09-05 with the real worker extractor: 28 future-dated events, 19 distinct titles. Examples it actually returned: "Reitturnier - Springen" "Erlebnis E-Bike Touren" "Alpakawanderung - Sommer". Read https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/de/kam/events.html (HTTP 200, 275,441 bytes) and the given https://www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com/en/kam/events.html (HTTP 200, 273,369 bytes); parsed 12 ld+json blocks on each. Actual ld+json entries: SportsEvent ''Reitturnier - Springen'' startDate 2026-09-05T09:00:00; Event ''KAISERLAN - Die LAN Party im Kaisersaal'' startDate 2026-09-05T00:00:00; Event ''Flohmarkt Kirchbichl'' startDate 2026-09-05T08:00:00, endDate 2026-09-05T14:00:00. Also Event ''WÖRGL farmer''s market'' 2026-09-05T08:30 → 12:30 and Event ''Führung durch das Wörgler Museum'' 2026-09-05T10:00 → 12:00. SECOND PASS CONFIRMED: Parsed the ld+json myself. Verbatim from the blocks: SportsEvent ''Reitturnier - Springen'', location ''Strasserwirt'', startDate 2026-09-05T09:00:00; Event ''KAISERLAN - Die LAN Party im Kaisersaal'', location ''Kaisersaal'', startDate 2026-09-05T00:00:00;…','www.kitzbueheler-alpen.com','src_bede9fe4',true,'jsonld'),
  ('Steiermark Tourismus (Steirische Tourismus und Standortmarketing GmbH — the Styria regional tourist board)','Steiermark','AT','https://www.steiermark.com/de/Urlaub-planen/Veranstaltungen','A filterable region-wide event calendar (11 sub-regions, 11 categories) whose result rows carry title, town, date range and start time as server-rendered HTML.',ARRAY['ausstellungen','musik','sport','feste / feiern','kulinarik & wein','theater / show / tanz / film / kleinkunst','volkskultur / brauchtum / märkte','familie'],'robots.txt fetched from https://www.steiermark.com/robots.txt on 2026-09-05 (HTTP 200). Rules read: User-agent: * / Allow: / / Disallow: /multimediaarchiv/ / Disallow: /*ajaxRequestType* / Disallow: /sk/* / Disallow: /it/* / Disallow: /fr/* / Disallow: /pl/* / Disallow: /sl/* / Disallow: /cs/* / Disallow: /nl/* / Disallow: /hu/* / Sitemap: https://www.steiermark.com/sitemap.site_6.xml / Sitemap: https://www.steiermark.com/sitemap.pressarticle.xml. The endpoint path is permitted, and no Crawl-delay is declared. https://www.steiermark.com/robots.txt: ''User-agent: *'' / ''Allow: /'', then ''Disallow: /multimediaarchiv/'', ''Disallow: /*ajaxRequestType*'' and language blocks ''Disallow: /sk/*'', ''/it/*'', ''/fr/*'', ''/pl/*'', ''/sl/*'', ''/cs/*'', ''/nl/*'', ''/hu/*''. Note the Hungarian tree /hu/ is disallowed — we must scrape /de/ (or /en/), never /hu/ — and the ''*ajaxRequestType*'' rule means the calendar''s…',1,'Measured locally on 2026-09-05 with the real worker extractor: 15 future-dated events, 12 distinct titles. Examples it actually returned: "Zeggern" "Jedermann" "EDLSEER Thermenfestival 2026 in Bad Waltersdorf". Read https://www.steiermark.com/de/Urlaub-planen/Veranstaltungen (HTTP 200, 470,315 bytes; ''355 Ergebnisse'', pager 1…30). Real titles with dates: ''Almabtrieb in Tragöß'' — Tragöß-Sankt Katharein, 05. Sep. 2026 von 09:00 Uhr; ''Jedermann Graz'' — Graz, 4.–06. Sep. 2026 von 20:00 Uhr; ''MEVZA Beach Volleyball Championships 2026'' — Schla